WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.867 --> 00:00:02.268 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Thank you so much.

00:00:02.268 --> 00:00:03.303
You gave me this earlier today,
and I´m really happy --

00:00:03.303 --> 00:00:04.571 align:start size:94% position:6%
What am I wearing from
the Whoopi line?

00:00:04.571 --> 00:00:06.639 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Short of wearing, you know,
Elf on a Shelf

00:00:06.639 --> 00:00:07.907 size:81% position:41%
and Mensch on a Bench.

00:00:07.907 --> 00:00:10.377 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, there you go.
That´s wonderful. Thank you.

00:00:10.377 --> 00:00:11.745
-Which is actually a doll that

00:00:11.745 --> 00:00:13.480 align:start size:94% position:6%
somebody made
a couple of years ago.

00:00:13.480 --> 00:00:15.882 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I just thought,
"Well, they should meet."

00:00:15.882 --> 00:00:17.684 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So, but this is
a passion of yours.

00:00:17.684 --> 00:00:18.885 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes.
-Holiday sweaters.

00:00:18.885 --> 00:00:19.986 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes.

00:00:19.986 --> 00:00:21.354 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You do not like them
to be called --

00:00:21.354 --> 00:00:23.156
You do not believe
these are ugly holiday sweaters.

00:00:23.156 --> 00:00:26.760
-No. I do believe they´re -- I
call them ugly holiday sweaters,

00:00:26.760 --> 00:00:27.961 align:start size:94% position:6%
and people keep saying,
"No, they´re not.

00:00:27.961 --> 00:00:29.029 size:81% position:41%
They´re really great."

00:00:29.029 --> 00:00:31.398 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I said, "Okay.
Whatever you like.

00:00:31.398 --> 00:00:33.233
They´re just holiday sweaters."

00:00:33.233 --> 00:00:34.567
-And do these help you --

00:00:34.567 --> 00:00:37.971
Do you find this helps you
with the holiday spirit?

00:00:37.971 --> 00:00:39.005 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No. You know what?

00:00:39.005 --> 00:00:40.740 align:start size:94% position:6%
I always have
the holiday spirit,

00:00:40.740 --> 00:00:45.445 align:start size:94% position:6%
because when I was a kid,
my mother made them magical.

00:00:45.445 --> 00:00:48.048 align:start size:94% position:6%
And so I was raised
to believe that children

00:00:48.048 --> 00:00:50.784 align:start size:94% position:6%
should have the holidays
to be children.

00:00:50.784 --> 00:00:53.119 align:start size:94% position:6%
They can be --
You know, you can mess them up

00:00:53.119 --> 00:00:55.321 align:start size:94% position:6%
any other time of the year,
but never during the holidays.

00:00:55.321 --> 00:00:57.190 align:start size:94% position:6%
-How did your mother
go about making it magical?

00:00:57.190 --> 00:01:01.561 align:start size:94% position:6%
What would she do?
-Well, so, you´d go to bed.

00:01:01.561 --> 00:01:05.298 size:84% position:42%
My brother and I had --
I had an older brother.

00:01:05.298 --> 00:01:08.068 align:start size:94% position:6%
And, so, we´d go to sleep
and we would wake up.

00:01:08.068 --> 00:01:10.670 align:start size:94% position:6%
And, in the old days,
there was this pink stuff

00:01:10.670 --> 00:01:13.239
that used to clean windows,
but every holiday season,

00:01:13.239 --> 00:01:14.707
they would give you stencils.

00:01:14.707 --> 00:01:16.643 size:88% position:44%
So, you´d stencil, like,

00:01:16.643 --> 00:01:19.045 align:start size:94% position:6%
a Christmas tree or
Christmas balls or whatever.

00:01:19.045 --> 00:01:20.980 align:start size:94% position:6%
And we´d wake up,
and there would be,

00:01:20.980 --> 00:01:22.348
like, stuff on the windows.

00:01:22.348 --> 00:01:24.584 align:start size:94% position:6%
And she would never say
anything about it.

00:01:24.584 --> 00:01:26.719 align:start size:94% position:6%
It was just, "Ooh!
Stuff is happening."

00:01:26.719 --> 00:01:29.556 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then, like,
a tree would appear.

00:01:29.556 --> 00:01:31.191 size:84% position:42%
And then, the next day,

00:01:31.191 --> 00:01:32.892 align:start size:94% position:6%
there would be
a couple things on the tree.

00:01:32.892 --> 00:01:34.761 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then there would be some
tinsel on the tree.

00:01:34.761 --> 00:01:39.232
And, so, up until Christmas Eve,
the tree got done,

00:01:39.232 --> 00:01:40.633
and she never said a word.

00:01:40.633 --> 00:01:42.569 align:start size:94% position:6%
It was like
it happened magically.

00:01:42.569 --> 00:01:45.071 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, wow. So you never saw
her doing any of it.

00:01:45.071 --> 00:01:46.573
-You never saw her doing it.

00:01:46.573 --> 00:01:48.808
And she would never say, "Oh,
what do you think of the tree?"

00:01:48.808 --> 00:01:50.677 align:start size:94% position:6%
She would just --
Everything that your mother

00:01:50.677 --> 00:01:52.278 align:start size:94% position:6%
would be doing normally,
she would be doing.

00:01:52.278 --> 00:01:54.447 align:start size:94% position:6%
And we would be like,
"What happened?!"

00:01:54.447 --> 00:01:56.216 align:start size:94% position:6%
How did this --"
Because, you know,

00:01:56.216 --> 00:02:00.253 align:start size:94% position:6%
I grew up in the projects,
so there was no chimney, okay?

00:02:00.253 --> 00:02:01.421 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, yeah.
-Yeah.

00:02:01.421 --> 00:02:02.989 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So when something gets
added to the tree,

00:02:02.989 --> 00:02:05.024
it means someone broke
into the apartment, yeah.

00:02:05.024 --> 00:02:09.596
-So, we then would go to sleep,
and it would be barren.

00:02:09.596 --> 00:02:11.564
It was just no toys or anything.

00:02:11.564 --> 00:02:13.967 align:start size:94% position:6%
And, man, we´d wake up
the next day,

00:02:13.967 --> 00:02:16.703 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I don´t know
where she hid everything.

00:02:16.703 --> 00:02:18.338
I don´t know how she did it,

00:02:18.338 --> 00:02:21.241 align:start size:94% position:6%
´cause she was
a really hard-working woman.

00:02:21.241 --> 00:02:23.243 align:start size:94% position:6%
But we had Christmas
like we were

00:02:23.243 --> 00:02:25.578 size:78% position:39%
the wealthiest people
in the world as kids.

00:02:25.578 --> 00:02:29.182 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I just think
that when someone --

00:02:29.182 --> 00:02:33.720
a parent or whoever the
person is that´s raising you --

00:02:33.720 --> 00:02:38.491 align:start size:94% position:6%
wants to make it
so much fun that you just --

00:02:38.491 --> 00:02:40.593
you never forget that feeling,

00:02:40.593 --> 00:02:42.762 align:start size:94% position:6%
you know, that smell,
for me turkey,

00:02:42.762 --> 00:02:46.065 align:start size:94% position:6%
and the smell of
the tree on Christmas morning.

00:02:46.065 --> 00:02:49.903
So, these are just meant to make
you smile and think,

00:02:49.903 --> 00:02:51.137 size:75% position:38%
"Hey, you know what?

00:02:51.137 --> 00:02:52.405 size:84% position:42%
Good times are coming."

00:02:52.405 --> 00:02:53.540 align:start size:94% position:6%
It´s hard.

00:02:53.540 --> 00:02:55.575 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, it´s hard
to keep chipper.

00:02:55.575 --> 00:02:57.510 align:start size:94% position:6%
But I think you have to
keep chipper for the kids.

00:02:57.510 --> 00:02:58.711 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.

00:02:58.711 --> 00:03:02.081 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You deserve --
Kids deserve a better time,

00:03:02.081 --> 00:03:03.550
sometimes, than we give them.

00:03:03.550 --> 00:03:05.618 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I just --
I think holidays do that.

00:03:05.618 --> 00:03:07.754 size:78% position:39%
And it doesn´t matter
what you celebrate.

00:03:07.754 --> 00:03:10.323 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, I´m trying
to hit everybody

00:03:10.323 --> 00:03:12.292 align:start size:94% position:6%
who´s celebrating
a holiday so that

00:03:12.292 --> 00:03:13.927
when we say "happy holidays" --

00:03:13.927 --> 00:03:15.929 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, you don´t walk up
and say, "Hey, are you Jewish?

00:03:15.929 --> 00:03:16.763 align:start size:94% position:6%
Happy Hanukkah.

00:03:16.763 --> 00:03:18.198
No. You say, "Happy holidays,

00:03:18.198 --> 00:03:20.033 align:start size:94% position:6%
´cause I don´t know
what you like."

00:03:20.033 --> 00:03:22.302 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-I don´t know what you like.

00:03:22.302 --> 00:03:24.671
I don´t know what you celebrate,
but happy whatever."

00:03:24.671 --> 00:03:26.439 align:start size:94% position:6%
So instead of saying
"happy whatever,"

00:03:26.439 --> 00:03:27.974 align:start size:94% position:6%
you say "happy holidays,"
which is nice.

00:03:27.974 --> 00:03:29.142 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It´s nice.

00:03:29.142 --> 00:03:30.677 align:start size:94% position:6%
It´s nice to cover everybody.
-I think so.

